.TH GUNTERDOWN 1 "October 2026" "Gunterdown 0.7.0"
.SH NAME
gunterdown \- multilingual Markdown terminal editor
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B gunterdown
[options] [file-or-directory]
.SH DESCRIPTION
A Python curses editor with Markdown highlighting, a file tree,
article templates, undo/redo, search and multilingual completion.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B --new FILE
Create an article using the template. Refuses an existing file.
.TP
.B -w, --workdir DIRECTORY
File tree root; file paths remain relative to the launch directory.
.TP
.B -l, --lang LANGUAGE
Force fr, en, ja, zh, ko, or auto detection.
.TP
.B --ui-lang LANGUAGE
Interface language: fr, en, ja, zh (Simplified Chinese), ko.
Independent of the completion language. Alt-U changes it in the editor.
.TP
.B --no-lang LANGUAGES
Disable comma-separated dictionaries.
.TP
.B --theme NAME
Choose dark, light, solarized, nord, dracula, ocean, contrast, or a custom theme.
Alt-Y opens the theme preview; Enter saves, Esc restores the previous theme.
.TP
.B --no-color
Disable colors.
.TP
.B --no-tree
Hide the file tree.
.TP
.B --template FILE
Use an alternative article template.
.TP
.B --diagnostics
Print and save diagnostic information.
.TP
.B -V, --version
Show version and available dictionaries.
.SH KEYS
Ctrl-S saves; Ctrl-X quits; Ctrl-U undoes; Ctrl-Y redoes;
F1 opens help; F2 opens menus; F9 toggles the tree.
Alt-B switches buffers; Alt-T inserts an article template.
.SH FILES
~/.config/gunterdown/config.json, keymap.json, recover/
.SH ENVIRONMENT
GUNTERDOWN_HOME, GUNTERDOWN_DICT_PATH, GUNTERDOWN_LANG, GUNTERDOWN_NO_COLOR.
.SH AUTHOR
Zeima. MIT license. Bundled demonstration lexicons are original data.
